url: "https://github.com/creelie/geometric-selection-conjecture"
abstract: "Explicit heterotic data tested against the Geometric Selection Conjecture: the generations, couplings and mass maps of the Dwork and weighted Fermat pencils, and the exclusion of three-family standard-embedding quotients of thirteen hypergeometric families. Every polystable sum of five line bundles with c_1 = 0 on a threefold with at most four Kahler parameters keeps a massless Abelian gauge boson; on a tetraquadric with a free (Z/2)^2 action extensions remove it, and one descends to the quotient with three families, one Higgs pair, no charged exotics and no extra gauge boson. No bundle on this quotient whose pullback is built by extensions from the eleven three-family line-bundle data has three Yukawa matrices of full rank at large volume. The conjecture is not proved."
date-released: "2026-10-30"
